From: X710 bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-geni: print the bus line levels when a transfer is NACKed

Every failed transfer on this board reports a bare -ENXIO, and that error has
two very different meanings: the slave did not acknowledge its address, or a bus
line is not idle.  The downstream driver this board's stock kernel uses
(i2c-msm-geni.c, CONFIG_I2C_MSM_GENI) separates them by reading SE_GENI_IOS
before every transfer and returning -ENXIO when SCL and SDA are not both high -
"IO lines in bad state, Power the slave".

Mainline reads the same register in geni_i2c_err_misc(), but that helper is only
called from the default branch of geni_i2c_err(): NACK and GENI_TIMEOUT - the two
cases this bring-up actually hits - are logged with dev_dbg and skip it, so the
line levels are never printed and the port's own gpio diagnostics cannot supply
them either, because gpio72 and gpio106 belong to the controller and read back
as -1.

Print the NACK/timeout message at info level, call geni_i2c_err_misc() for it,
and spell out the verdict for SE_GENI_IOS.  The check, the error codes and the
recovery path are unchanged: this only makes an existing measurement visible.
---
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
index d2f5055b0..fe2c5dd17 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
@@ -234,10 +234,17 @@ static void geni_i2c_err_misc(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c)
 		rx_st = readl_relaxed(gi2c->se.base + SE_GENI_RX_FIFO_STATUS);
 		tx_st = readl_relaxed(gi2c->se.base + SE_GENI_TX_FIFO_STATUS);
 	}
-	dev_dbg(gi2c->se.dev, "DMA:%d tx_stat:0x%x, rx_stat:0x%x, irq-stat:0x%x\n",
-		dma, tx_st, rx_st, m_stat);
-	dev_dbg(gi2c->se.dev, "m_cmd:0x%x, geni_status:0x%x, geni_ios:0x%x\n",
-		m_cmd, geni_s, geni_ios);
+	/*
+	 * Bits 0 and 1 of SE_GENI_IOS are the SDA and SCL line levels: 0x3 means
+	 * both are high, i.e. an idle bus, so a failure is a real address NACK;
+	 * anything else means something is holding a line down.
+	 */
+	dev_info(gi2c->se.dev, "DMA:%d tx_stat:0x%x, rx_stat:0x%x, irq-stat:0x%x\n",
+		 dma, tx_st, rx_st, m_stat);
+	dev_info(gi2c->se.dev, "m_cmd:0x%x, geni_status:0x%x, geni_ios:0x%x (%s)\n",
+		 m_cmd, geni_s, geni_ios,
+		 (geni_ios & 0x3) == 0x3 ? "scl/sda high, idle bus" :
+					   "scl/sda NOT both high");
 }
 
 static void geni_i2c_err(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c, int err)
@@ -254,7 +261,14 @@ static void geni_i2c_err(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c, int err)
 		break;
 	case NACK:
 	case GENI_TIMEOUT:
-		dev_dbg(gi2c->se.dev, "%s\n", gi2c_log[err].msg);
+		/*
+		 * NACK is the common case on a bring-up board and the one case
+		 * that says nothing about *why*: the same -ENXIO is returned when
+		 * the slave does not acknowledge its address and when a line is
+		 * held down.  Print it, and print the line levels with it.
+		 */
+		dev_info(gi2c->se.dev, "%s\n", gi2c_log[err].msg);
+		geni_i2c_err_misc(gi2c);
 		break;
 	default:
 		dev_err(gi2c->se.dev, "%s\n", gi2c_log[err].msg);
